From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: en751221: raise WAN QDMA congestion thresholds

Upstream FoE flows reach the WAN QDMA from a 1 Gbit/s LAN port, but GPON
grants drain them only in bursts. With the thresholds captured from the
shipping firmware (total min 819, channel min 160, queue 24..819), the
dynamic congestion control drops about 0.9 % of a saturated upload at
the hardware forwarding ingress (CDMA2_RXHWF_DROP_CNT). The PPE, the
switches and the GPON MAC lose nothing, so these drops are the whole
TCP loss. They halve the upload of higher-RTT clients such as WiFi
stations.

Raise the minimum thresholds so line-rate bursts fit: total min 4096,
channel min 2048 and queue 2048..4095. The drops and the dynamic
control stay enabled, so the queue stays within the 4096 descriptor
pool and a stalled GPON link cannot back-pressure the frame engine.

Measured on a TP-Link Archer XR500v (Movistar GPON) with a saturated
4-stream upload: HWF ingress drops go from 0.90 % to 0.19 % with the
same throughput, and the loaded RTT goes from 30 to ~35 ms. A WiFi
laptop's upload against a single server goes from ~300 to 554 Mbit/s.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1686,11 +1686,24 @@
 		queue_max = 204;
 	} else if (qdma->fwd_buf_size == 2048 && qdma->qdma->id == 1 &&
 		   qdma->num_fwd_descs == 4096) {
-		total_min = 819;
+		/*
+		 * Upstream FoE flows enter this QDMA from a 1 Gbit/s LAN port
+		 * and leave through GPON grants that drain at the line rate
+		 * only in bursts. With the shipping thresholds (total min 819,
+		 * channel min 160, queue 24..819) the dynamic congestion
+		 * control drops ~0.9 % of a saturated upload at the HWF ingress
+		 * (CDMA2_RXHWF_DROP_CNT), which halves TCP throughput for
+		 * higher-RTT clients. Raise the minimum thresholds so line-rate
+		 * bursts fit, while keeping the queue well inside the 4096
+		 * descriptor pool and the drops enabled, so a stalled GPON
+		 * link cannot back-pressure the frame engine.
+		 */
+		total_min = 4096;
 		total_max = 15360;
-		channel_min = 160;
+		channel_min = 2048;
 		channel_max = 15360;
-		queue_max = 819;
+		queue_min = 2048;
+		queue_max = 4095;
 	}
 
 	airoha_wr((void __iomem *)&qdma->regs->tx_congest_thr, 0,
